# C++

When editing matching files:

- Apply engineering foundations first (always-applied rule).
- Load `skills/code/languages/cpp/SKILL.md` for language rules.
- Load its `references/` only when the skill directs (including `references/tooling.md` when CMake, tidy, sanitizers, or the dependency manifest come up).
- Follow the nearest `AGENT.md` chain for Validate commands and the project C++ standard.

Key rules: honest types (no `void*` / C-style casts), no diagnostic suppression, RAII (no raw `new`/`delete`), explicit ownership at signatures, fail-fast status types, no `printf`/`std::cout` in shipped code.
